class: divergence
divergence.broiler-js: Number::toString at a radix other than 10 gives a wrong value for a magnitude of 2^63 or more: the integer part is converted through a 64-bit integer. Answered by Broiler.JS docs/roadmap/SharedLibraries.md, item SJL-3 (the number-conversion cut-over).
divergence.broiler-vm: Number::toString at a radix other than 10 gives integer digits that do not denote the value at a magnitude of 2^53 or more: the integer part is divided by the radix in double arithmetic, which is inexact there. Answered by Broiler.VM docs/javascript-shared-libraries/milestones/sjl-3-number-conversion-pilot.md, SJL-3.4 (Broiler.VM's cut-over).
