in: f64:0x3FE0000000000000 int:17
out: value: str:"0.8888888888889"
class: divergence
divergence.broiler-js: Number::toString at a radix other than 10 gives more digits than the shortest that round-trip: the fraction is expanded digit by digit (up to 1,100 digits) instead of stopping at the shortest. Answered by Broiler.JS docs/roadmap/SharedLibraries.md, item SJL-3 (the number-conversion cut-over).
divergence.broiler-vm: Number::toString at a radix other than 10 gives fraction digits that do not denote the value: the expansion stops at half the gap to the next double above, computed in double arithmetic, which is not the specification's criterion. Answered by Broiler.VM docs/javascript-shared-libraries/milestones/sjl-3-number-conversion-pilot.md, SJL-3.4 (Broiler.VM's cut-over).
