class: divergence
divergence.broiler-js: Number::toString at a radix other than 10 gives digits that do not denote the value: the fraction is expanded in double arithmetic, whose rounding error enters the digits. Answered by Broiler.JS docs/roadmap/SharedLibraries.md, item SJL-3 (the number-conversion cut-over).
divergence.broiler-vm: Number::toString at a radix other than 10 gives fraction digits that do not denote the value: the expansion stops at half the gap to the next double above, computed in double arithmetic, which is not the specification's criterion. Answered by Broiler.VM docs/javascript-shared-libraries/milestones/sjl-3-number-conversion-pilot.md, SJL-3.4 (Broiler.VM's cut-over).
