id: numbers/to-string-radix-arguments/0002
area: numbers
op: Number.prototype.toString
in: f64:0x4014000000000000 int:0
out: error: RangeError
class: divergence
divergence.broiler-js: Number.prototype.toString takes a radix whose ToIntegerOrInfinity is 0 (0, null, -0) as radix 10, and a NaN radix escapes as a host ArgumentException, where each is a RangeError. Answered by Broiler.JS docs/roadmap/SharedLibraries.md, item SJL-3 (the number-conversion cut-over).
prov: spec:es2026@0248456c#sec-number.prototype.tostring ref:numref@1
script: $f64(0x40140000, 0x00000000).toString(0)
since: 1

